# ndeko harness — .gitignore
#
# This tree is meant to be clonable and to stay CLEAN during normal operation.
# The system it replaces left session runtime untracked-but-not-ignored, so the
# working tree was permanently dirty (8 of 14 dirty entries at audit time were
# session state). Everything the harness writes at runtime belongs here.

# ─── Secrets. Never in this repo, even ignored. Canonical home is the data tree.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Dependencies
node_modules/
bun.lockb

# ─── Session + agent runtime (the dirty-tree class)
teams/
daemon/
daemon.lock
daemon.status.json
daemon.log
jobs/
bridge-spawn/
*.lock
.last_inuse_sweep
.last-update-result.json

# ─── Harness-managed runtime state
# .claude.json and backups/ are created the first time the harness runs against
# this config dir — found by running `claude auto-mode config` and watching the
# tree go dirty, which is exactly the class this section exists to prevent.
.claude.json
.claude.json.backup
backups/
projects/
plugins/cache/
plugins/data/
plugins/marketplaces/
plugins/*.json
# The server-side skill and plugin sync cache. Keyed by an account/org bucket
# (`<uuid>_<uuid>/`), refilled by the harness on every sync, and holding
# org-library content that belongs to the org rather than to this repo. A
# blanket `git add -A` swept 222 of these files into the index on 2026-09-18,
# which is how they were found.
plugins/synced/
skills/synced/
shell-snapshots/
statsig/
todos/
history.jsonl
remote-settings.json
policy-limits.json
# Sibling of the above. `policy-limits.json` was ignored; this stamp was not,
# and it carries an org identity hash -- data-shaped, so it stays local.
policy-limits.json.stamp.json
stats-cache.json
settings.local.json
mcp-needs-auth-cache.json
gh-pr-status-cache.json
.last-cleanup

# ─── Per-session runtime. Same class as teams/ above, found the same way.
# These hold transcripts, pasted content, and file snapshots — personal data by
# definition, in a repo whose rule is that none belongs here. `tasks/` and
# `session-env/` were invisible at audit time only because git does not track
# empty directories; they would have appeared with the first file written.
sessions/
tasks/
session-env/
file-history/
# `feedback/` holds locally-queued product-feedback drafts, which quote the
# session verbatim and carry absolute paths. Found the way the two above were:
# the privacy gate refused a commit that had swept it in. `ide/` is the same
# class and was invisible for the same reason -- git does not track an empty
# directory, so it had never appeared in `git status`.
feedback/
ide/

# ─── Generated Python venv for the Chatterbox voice toolchain (~1.3G).
# The source (chatterbox, cli.py, setup.sh) IS tracked; the venv is rebuilt by
# setup.sh on first run. Ignored because pushing 1.3G of wheels to a git remote
# is the kind of mistake that is very annoying to undo.
tools/chatterbox/venv/

# ─── Generated venv + model weights for the Kokoro TTS toolchain (~500M).
# Same rule as chatterbox above: the source (kokoro, cli.py, setup.sh) IS
# tracked, the venv and the .onnx weights are rebuilt by setup.sh on first
# run. The models are third-party release assets, not harness content.
tools/kokoro/venv/
tools/kokoro/models/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ─── Caches the harness fills in the background.
cache/
paste-cache/
image-cache/
chrome/

# ─── Logs. daemon.log is listed above; this catches the rest, including the
# git-push launchd logs that grow continuously.
*.log

# ─── Local settings overlay (machine-specific, not portable)
settings.user.json

# ─── Private skills.
# The leading underscore is the public/private boundary. These encode customer
# or employer specifics — real customer IDs, internal org structure, account
# names — so they live on this machine and load normally, but never enter the
# repo. A fresh clone gets the harness without them, which is correct: that
# tooling shouldn't travel.
skills/_*/

# ─── Anything data-shaped that leaks in by accident.
# The data tree lives outside this repo on purpose; these are tripwires.
memory/
identity/
goals.md
state/

# ─── OS noise
.DS_Store

# Symlinks into a local Interceptor checkout. Their targets are absolute paths on
# one machine, so they stay untracked; recreate them per machine.
skills/interceptor-browser
skills/interceptor-macos
skills/interceptor-research
